# dev.env — your own defaults for the make targets. Copy this file to dev.env
# (git-ignored) and uncomment what you want; `make VAR=value` still wins.
# Plain KEY=value lines, no `export`, no quotes.

# Vite dev server port, for `make web`, `make debug` and `make ios-live`.
# WEB_PORT=5173

# `make web` binds here; 0.0.0.0 lets a phone on the LAN load the game.
# WEB_HOST=localhost

# Main-process inspector port for `make debug`; DEVTOOLS=1 opens DevTools.
# INSPECT=9229
# DEVTOOLS=0

# `make ios`: the simulator to use, by name (`make ios-list`), or a phone by
# udid. PHONE is what `make ios-phone` uses.
# IOS_SIM=iPhone 17 Pro
# DEVICE=
# PHONE=<udid of your iPhone, from make ios-list>
